.TH CHONK 1 "2025" "ChonkOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
chonk \- system maintenance for ChonkOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chonk
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chonk
performs maintenance tasks on a ChonkOS system: health checks, APT updates,
cache cleaning, profile switching, and access to bundled
tool documentation.
Exit status is 0 on success and 1 on any error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Print machine-readable JSON on stdout instead of a table.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Check system health: ChonkOS os-release ID, chonkos-system sysctl drop-in
(warning only), APT sources, keyring, ZRAM swap (/dev/zram0), root disk usage
(warning above 85%), and failed systemd units.
Exits 1 if any check fails.
.TP
.BR update " [\fB\-\-yes\fR]"
Run apt-get update, upgrade, and autoremove. Requires root; exits 1 otherwise.
Without \fB\-\-yes\fR, apt prompts interactively.
.TP
.BR clean " [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-dev\fR]"
Without \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR (requires root): apt-get clean, apt-get autoremove,
journalctl \-\-vacuum-size=50M. \fB\-\-dev\fR also scans $HOME for stale
(>30 days) target/ and node_modules/ directories; without \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
each removal asks for y/N confirmation.
.TP
.BR profile " <\fIdev|battery|homelab|status\fR> [\fB\-\-dark\fR]"
Show or change the active ChonkOS profile. \fIdev\fR, \fIbattery\fR and
\fIhomelab\fR require root: they set the lid switch action (suspend, or ignore
for \fIhomelab\fR), apply the matching TLP mode (ac, or bat for \fIbattery\fR),
and record the profile in /var/lib/chonkos/profile. \fB\-\-dark\fR additionally
runs \fBnap dark on\fR. The lid drop-in is reloaded, never restarted.
\fIstatus\fR prints the current profile, lid actions, TLP mode, CPU scaling
governor and ZRAM state. \fB\-\-json\fR is supported for both.
.TP
.BR card " [\fB\-\-plain\fR]"
Print a system card: release and kernel versions, uptime, PSS across readable
processes, ZRAM usage and compression, boot time or load average, battery and
thermal readings, wildcard/loopback listeners and the latest seal.
\fB\-\-plain\fR suppresses the terminal illustration and colors. With
\fB\-\-json\fR the output carries schema_version 1 and an RFC 3339 UTC
timestamp.
.TP
.BR try " [\fB\-\-label\fR NAME] \fB\-\-\fR COMMAND [ARG...]"
Create a seal, run COMMAND synchronously, show the changes and print the
restore preview command. In JSON mode the child output goes to stderr and
stdout carries the JSON result. The seal store must be writable by the
invoking user.
.TP
.BR docs " [\fItool\fR]"
Print the bundled tools documentation from
.IR /usr/share/doc/chonkos-tools/TOOLS.md .
With \fItool\fR (chonk, scale, nap, whisker or seal), print only that tool's
section; unknown names exit 1.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
chonk doctor
.TP
chonk --json doctor
.TP
sudo chonk update --yes
.TP
sudo chonk clean --dry-run --dev
.TP
sudo chonk profile battery
.TP
sudo chonk profile battery --dark
.TP
chonk profile status
.TP
chonk card --plain
.TP
chonk --json card
.TP
sudo chonk try --label "upgrade" -- apt-get upgrade
.TP
chonk docs scale
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/chonkos-tools/TOOLS.md
Bundled tools documentation.
.TP
.I /var/lib/chonkos/profile
Active ChonkOS profile.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/chonkos.sources
ChonkOS APT repository configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/share/keyrings/chonkos.gpg
ChonkOS APT repository keyring.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scale (1)
